/*
 * diagnostic — the sink of the non fatal diagnostics.
 *
 * An ErrorMsg is raised by the compiler in two ways: it is thrown, aborting
 * the compilation, or it is reported, printed and left behind while the
 * compilation carries on. This module owns that decision, so that severity is
 * read back in a single place rather than at every raise site.
 *
 * A warning is only non fatal in debug mode. Everywhere else it still aborts,
 * as it always did.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::errors::diagnostic
 * @File: ymirc/errors/diagnostic.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-09
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
